        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Minh Diep",
          "email": "mdiep@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-08-07 19:19:49.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20560 contrib: make checkpatch man4 nag satisfiable",
        "message": "LU-20560 contrib: make checkpatch man4 nag satisfiable\n\nThe LUSTRE_{RO,RW,WO}_ATTR spelling.txt entries nag every new sysfs\nparameter to add a Documentation/man4/ page, but fire on the macro\ntoken unconditionally: with CI gating on warnings, a patch adding a\nparameter fails whether or not the page exists. Suppress the warning\nwhen a matching Documentation/man4/<name>.4 page is present, so the\ncheck enforces what it claims to enforce.\n\nA page added by the same patch that adds the LUSTRE_*_ATTR() using\nit isn't on disk yet when checkpatch reads a bare patch, which is\nhow contrib/scripts/gerrit_checkpatch.py invokes it in CI (patch\npiped on stdin, no working tree checked out) -- the main case this\nchange is meant to unblock. Pre-scan the patch for any\nDocumentation/man4/*.4 hunks it adds and accept those too. Also\nanchor the on-disk lookup to checkpatch.pl's own directory instead\nof the current working directory, since the lookup was silently\ninert whenever checkpatch ran from anywhere but the tree root.\n\nMODULE_PARM_DESC and LDEBUGFS_SEQ_FOPS_* carry the same unsatisfiable\n\"create Documentation/man4/ page\" text and take the parameter name\nthe same way, so extend the same tree/patch lookup to them instead\nof leaving them nagging unconditionally.\n\nAlso exempt the spelling dictionaries from their own typo scan --\nany addition to spelling-userspace.txt used to trip its own entry,\nso the dictionary could never be extended through a warnings-gated\nCI. Anchor the exemption to contrib/scripts/spelling*.txt instead of\nany path containing \"scripts/spelling\", which exempted more than\nintended.\n\nTLC-bug-id: TLU-208\n\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5d4fe5e7a2e2474dfa98e992034a54ff92f1f2c3\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
